{
  "title": "Programmatic Marketing Engine — Event Bus, MCP Tool Layer, Multi-Agent Runtime, HITL Gate",
  "platform": "n8n",
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "bus",
      "label": "1 · EVENT BUS",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Every source posts into one bus rather than each integration owning its own trigger. Events are normalized to a single schema and stamped with an idempotency key, so a replayed webhook from Meta or a duplicate CRM fire costs nothing. This is the piece that makes 14 verticals additive instead of multiplicative."
    },
    {
      "key": "agents",
      "label": "2 · MULTI-AGENT RUNTIME",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "One agent per domain, each holding only the tools for its domain. Agents propose actions, they do not execute them. Separating proposal from execution is what makes an autonomous ad-spend system safe to run, and it is the reason a budget agent cannot touch the CMS."
    },
    {
      "key": "mcp",
      "label": "3 · MCP TOOL LAYER",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Each platform is exposed as an MCP server rather than hard-wired into a workflow. The tool contract is the integration, so swapping Google Ads for another channel, or reusing the CRM server in a different agent, is a config change. This is the layer the retainer maintains."
    },
    {
      "key": "gate",
      "label": "4 · GOVERNANCE GATE",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Every proposed action carries an estimated cost and blast radius before anything runs. Inside policy it executes automatically. Outside policy, above a spend cap, or touching published content, it queues for a human with the diff attached. Nothing bypasses this node."
    },
    {
      "key": "observe",
      "label": "5 · EXECUTE & OBSERVE",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Execution happens through the same MCP tools the agents proposed against, so the audit trail is one record. Token spend, API cost and outcome are written to a ledger on every run, which is what turns cost tracking into a dashboard instead of a monthly surprise."
    }
  ],
